      "candidateCard": "Acknowledge the cost plainly rather than moving past it, and ask what would be manageable rather than assuming.\n\nSeparate the plan honestly into what must be done now, what should be done within months, and what can wait a year or more.\n\nExplain what happens to each of the untreated teeth over that time, specifically rather than as a general warning about neglect.\n\nExplain the cheaper interim options that are genuinely available: a temporary dressing, a simple filling now with a better restoration later, and extraction where a tooth is beyond saving.\n\nExplain the funding routes: what is available under the health service where he is, payment plans, and any local scheme, and be specific about what each covers.\n\nAsk about his circumstances only as far as is needed to check whether he may be exempt from charges or entitled to help.\n\nOffer a staged plan with dates, so that he leaves with a sequence rather than a total figure.\n\nDeal with the embarrassment directly and briefly, and make clear that this conversation happens often and changes nothing about his care.\n\nAsk what he can do himself in the meantime that costs nothing — the brushing, the interdental cleaning, the sugar and the fluoride toothpaste — and be specific rather than general.\n\nAgree what will happen at the next appointment and what it will cost, exactly, so there is no surprise."
