      "patientConcern": "Behind the request is repeated pain, repeated cost, and a belief that dentures are an ending rather than another set of problems.",
      "prepSeconds": 180,
      "speakSeconds": 300,
      "candidateCard": "Ask her to tell you what has brought her to this, and let the whole story come out before you respond to any part of it.\n\nFind out what she believes dentures would solve: the pain, the cost, the appointments, the appearance, or the worry.\n\nExplain honestly what her mouth is actually like now: which teeth need what, which are sound, and that none of them is beyond saving.\n\nBe honest about full dentures, particularly the lower one: that the lower ridge shrinks over the years, that a lower denture is often loose, and that this is anatomy rather than a matter of getting a better one made.\n\nExplain what cannot be undone: that once the teeth are out, the bone changes permanently and the options narrow.\n\nAsk about her mother's experience specifically, since that is the picture she is working from, and find out what she actually saw.\n\nOffer the middle ground she may not know about: treating the worst teeth first, a partial denture, a staged plan over a year, and what each would cost.\n\nAsk whether the cost or the pain is the bigger problem, because the answer changes which plan is right.\n\nAgree that no decision is made today, offer her time and a written plan, and make clear that you will not refuse her outright if she still wants it after understanding all of it."
