      "prepSeconds": 180,
      "speakSeconds": 300,
      "candidateCard": "Thank her for making the referral, and ask her to describe what happens at a typical mealtime from start to finish, before you offer anything that you saw yourself.\n\nAsk what the resident used to enjoy eating, who in the home knew her before she became unwell, and whether anybody has asked her family about it.\n\nReport what you observed neutrally: the noise, the plate, the cutlery, the position, the timing and what was taken away.\n\nExplain what each of those does to intake, and pick the two that would make the biggest difference with no extra staff time.\n\nExplain the difference between a resident who refuses and a resident who cannot start, cannot see the food, or cannot use the cutlery, and how to tell them apart.\n\nExplain what finger food would do here, with specific examples the kitchen can provide, and why it often works when a plate and cutlery do not.\n\nDeal with the supplement request honestly: what supplements can and cannot do, why food first comes first, and what you will prescribe and when.\n\nAsk what would make this possible on a shift, and shape the plan around eleven residents rather than one.\n\nAsk what has already been tried for this resident and what happened, so that nothing is suggested twice.\n\nAgree what the home will do this week, what will be recorded, and when you will come back — and offer to speak to the manager about the mealtime yourself."
