      "patientConcern": "He believes he is being punished or rationed, and he has been told nothing except that he is on a \"special diet\".",
      "prepSeconds": 180,
      "speakSeconds": 300,
      "candidateCard": "Ask what he has been told so far by anybody on the ward, and be honest with him if the answer turns out to be that nobody has explained any of it.\n\nApologise plainly that he has been on a restricted intake for two days without anybody explaining to him what it was for.\n\nExplain what happens to a body after weeks with very little food, and why suddenly eating a full amount can be dangerous — in ordinary words, not in the language of electrolytes.\n\nExplain what the daily blood tests are for and what you are watching, and tell him today's results.\n\nBe specific about the timescale: what he is having today, what increases tomorrow, and roughly when he will be eating normally.\n\nExplain the supplements he is being given — the thiamine and the vitamins — and why those are not optional.\n\nTake the hunger seriously: what he can have safely between the planned amounts, and what he cannot.\n\nAsk what he actually wants to eat, and get as much of it as possible into the plan.\n\nAsk what will happen when he leaves, since eight weeks without food had a cause, and make sure that somebody is dealing with it before he goes.\n\nAsk him to tell you back what will change tomorrow, so that you both know he has been given a plan rather than a restriction."
