      "candidateCard": "Ask him to show you how he usually moves his wife and how many times a day he does it, and let him describe his own back before you say anything about it.\n\nExplain plainly what the underarm lift does: the nerves and the shoulder joint that are unprotected there, and that a shoulder can be dislocated by exactly that hold in someone with a weak arm.\n\nExplain what it is doing to his own back, and what happens to his wife if he is the one who ends up unable to lift anything.\n\nFind out what he thinks the hoist would mean — for her dignity, for the time it takes, and for what he believes about himself as her husband — and answer each of those separately.\n\nOffer the smaller step: a handling belt for the transfers she can help with, and the hoist only for the ones she cannot, rather than all or nothing.\n\nOffer a demonstration with somebody who will come and show him properly, at a time when his daughter can be there too.\n\nBe honest about what you must record and what you must pass on, and why, so that nothing arrives as a surprise.\n\nAgree exactly what will happen before your next visit and what he is willing to try in the meantime."
