      "prepSeconds": 180,
      "speakSeconds": 300,
      "candidateCard": "Thank him for telling you to your face rather than simply not coming back next week, and mean it when you say it.\n\nAsk what he has found useful and what he has not, session by session rather than in general.\n\nAsk specifically about week three, since that is where his attendance changed, and give him room to answer honestly.\n\nIf the reading aloud comes up, acknowledge it plainly and say what you would do differently, without defending the exercise.\n\nAsk what he was hoping for when he agreed to come, and whether any of that has happened.\n\nBe honest about what the group can and cannot offer, and do not oversell the remaining four sessions.\n\nOffer the alternatives: individual sessions, a different group, a work placement, or a pause with an open door.\n\nAsk what he wants to happen next with the work goal itself, since that has not changed even if the group is wrong for him.\n\nAsk what he would say to somebody else thinking of joining the group, since that usually gets a more honest answer than asking about himself.\n\nAsk what has been happening outside the group over these four weeks — the sleep, the days, the money — since that may matter more than the sessions.\n\nAgree the next step, put a date on it, and make clear that stopping the group is not stopping the service."
