      "prepSeconds": 180,
      "speakSeconds": 300,
      "candidateCard": "Explain what you measured today and what the legal standard actually is, using both numbers, and show him the number plate result from the car park rather than describing it to him.\n\nState plainly that he does not meet the standard, that he must not drive home today, and that he must inform the licensing authority himself.\n\nExplain that this is a measurement against a published standard rather than your opinion of him or of his driving.\n\nDeal with the argument he will make — local roads, daylight, sixty years without an accident — with what the measurement actually means for stopping distance and for a child stepping out.\n\nRaise the insurance position and what a refused claim would mean, because it is often the point that lands when nothing else does.\n\nExplain what could change it: the cataract surgery he has twice declined, what it would involve, and what vision he could reasonably expect afterwards.\n\nAsk about his wife's appointments specifically, and treat that as the problem to be solved rather than as an excuse.\n\nOffer the practical routes: hospital transport, community transport, the voluntary car scheme, and a referral to social care for her.\n\nTell him honestly what you are obliged to do if he continues to drive, and that you would tell him before doing it rather than going behind his back.\n\nAgree how he gets home today, and offer to telephone somebody for him yourself."
