      "candidateCard": "Ask what she has already tried, where the exercises came from, how she did them, and for how long.\n\nAsk specifically about her sleep: which side she lies on, whether she wakes, and how long she has been like this.\n\nExplain what the condition actually is, in plain words, and why it is a loading problem rather than an inflammatory one.\n\nExplain honestly what an injection does and how long it lasts, and what the evidence shows at three months and at twelve months compared with an exercise programme.\n\nBe clear that you are not refusing the injection: explain who would decide, and that it can be combined with the programme rather than replacing it.\n\nExplain why the exercises she found online may not have worked: the type, the load, the frequency, and the positions that provoke this particular tendon.\n\nGive her the things that will change her nights this week: how to lie, the pillow between the knees, avoiding crossing her legs, and not lying on the painful side.\n\nSet out the programme with numbers and an honest timescale, including when she should expect a change and what will happen before then.\n\nAsk what she most wants to be able to do again, so that the programme has a target she cares about rather than a range of movement.\n\nAgree the review point at which, if there has been no change, you will support her request for the injection."
