      "candidateCard": "Ask how he is, and check the specific things — the elbow, his head, his hip, any pain anywhere — and what he remembers.\n\nSay plainly what happened and that it happened while he was in your care, and apologise without qualifying it.\n\nStop him apologising to you, and say clearly that this was not his fault and not a sign that he cannot do this.\n\nExplain what has already been done: the doctor's review, the dressing, the x-ray request, and the observations that will be taken.\n\nExplain what will be recorded: the incident form, the notes, and that his family will be told — and ask whether he would like to tell them himself.\n\nDeal with the confidence directly, because the loss of it is the injury that will cost him most:\nexplain what usually happens after a fall in rehabilitation and what you will do differently.\n\nAgree what happens at the next session: a shorter distance, a second person, a belt, and the same walk he was doing when he fell rather than a different one.\n\nExplain honestly what would happen if he refuses to walk again, in terms of what he came in for.\n\nAgree a time to walk again — today or tomorrow rather than next week — and ask him what would make him willing to try it again."
