      "prepSeconds": 180,
      "speakSeconds": 300,
      "candidateCard": "Thank her for bringing her mother and ask how the appointment went from her side.\n\nExplain honestly what your role is: that you take the images and that a radiologist reports them.\n\nExplain that you are not able to give an opinion on what the images show, and why that is about accuracy rather than secrecy.\n\nCorrect the point about the power of attorney kindly: explain the difference between a financial attorney and one for health and welfare, and ask which she holds.\n\nAsk what her mother has said about sharing information with her, and whether she has been involved in her mother's care up to now.\n\nExplain who will have the result, when, and how it usually reaches the family.\n\nAsk what she is most worried about, since the answer may be something you can address today.\n\nTell her what she can do now: speak to the referring team, ask the ward or the doctor's secretary, and who to ask for by name.\n\nExplain how to request the images and the report formally, for the future, and roughly how long that takes.\n\nCheck on the practical things: how they are getting home, whether her mother is settled, and whether she needs a chair or a drink.\n\nGive her the department's number and a name, so that she is not starting from the beginning next time."
