      "candidateCard": "Ask how she is, four weeks on, and how much she wants to talk about today.\n\nAsk who is at home with her and who came with her to the clinic today.\n\nAsk what she has been told about her speech, and what she has noticed herself.\n\nAsk permission before you raise the subject, and say what the subject is before she agrees.\n\nExplain what voice banking is in plain words, and what she would end up with.\n\nBe honest about why it is being raised now: that it needs a voice that still sounds like hers, and that this is the reason for the timing rather than any prediction about her.\n\nExplain what doing it involves: the recording, the number of sentences, how long it takes, and that it can be done in short sessions at home.\n\nBe honest that some people choose not to, and that this is a real choice rather than a formality.\n\nAsk what she would want a recorded voice for, and let her answer shape what is recorded.\n\nExplain the alternatives if she decides against it, so the choice is not between banking and nothing.\n\nCheck what support she has and who she would tell about this conversation.\n\nAgree what happens next: information to take away, a date to decide by, and who to contact when she is ready."
