      "candidateCard": "Ask her to tell you what a normal day looks like, and let her say what she is actually doing rather than what she thinks she should say.\n\nAsk what he says about the thickened drinks, and what happened the first time she gave him tea.\n\nThank her for telling you the truth, and say plainly that you would rather know than have a plan on the wall that nobody follows.\n\nAsk what she has noticed when he drinks tea: coughing, a wet voice afterwards, or nothing at all.\n\nExplain what happens when fluid goes the wrong way, and be honest that it does not always cause coughing.\n\nExplain what a chest infection would mean for him at 79, without predicting it as a certainty.\n\nExplore what can be changed rather than repeating the instruction: the brand of thickener, the temperature, the strength, and whether pre-thickened drinks would taste better to him.\n\nAsk whether he was part of the decision six weeks ago, and whether anyone asked him what he wanted.\n\nExplain that he is entitled to choose the risk himself if he understands it, and what that would involve rather than presenting it as a loophole.\n\nAgree what happens today: which drinks stay thickened, which do not, and what she will watch for.\n\nArrange to come back and review it with both of them together, so the plan belongs to them."
