      "candidateCard": "Give the result clearly in one sentence, including the numbers, and then stop.\n\nLet him react, and do not fill the silence with procedure.\n\nGo through the animals individually: which cows, their ear numbers, and what the readings were.\n\nAsk what has changed on the farm in the last year: bought-in stock, contractors, shared grazing, and the neighbouring herds.\n\nAsk when the last test was, and whether anything about this one was different in his eyes.\n\nExplain what the test measures and, honestly, what its limitations are, without encouraging him to dismiss the result.\n\nExplain exactly what happens next and when: the restriction, the notification, the removal of the reactors, and who does each of those things.\n\nExplain the position of the inconclusive animals separately, since they are not the same as the reactors.\n\nExplain the retest interval and be honest that you cannot predict what it will show.\n\nDeal with the practical consequences he is thinking about: movements, sales, milk, and the calves.\n\nTalk about compensation and where he will find out what it will be, without guessing at figures, and tell him who values the animals and when.\n\nRaise the biosecurity questions that will matter for the next test, and agree which of them to look at first.\n\nAsk who else needs to be told today, offer to speak to anyone he wants, and arrange to come back this week."
