      "candidateCard": "Ask about the cough: when it started, what brings it on, whether anything comes up, and whether the dog is otherwise himself.\n\nAsk about the kennels, other dogs, and his vaccination history.\n\nAsk whether any of the other dogs there are coughing, and whether he has met any dogs since coming home.\n\nAsk whether the dog has ever had anything like this before, and what was given then.\n\nExamine the dog thoroughly and say your findings out loud as you go.\n\nExplain what you think this is and why the findings point that way.\n\nExplain what is most likely causing it and why an antibiotic would not treat that.\n\nBe honest about the exceptions: what would make antibiotics appropriate, and what you would look for.\n\nAddress the suspicion directly and say plainly that this is not about cost.\n\nExplain what antibiotic resistance means in practical terms for his own dog in future, briefly and without a lecture.\n\nGive him a real plan: rest, a harness instead of a collar, avoiding smoke and dust, and how long this usually takes.\n\nBe specific about what would mean coming back: a temperature, going off food, breathlessness, lethargy, or a cough that is worse after five days.\n\nOffer a telephone review rather than a second journey, and make sure he leaves with the plan written down."
